+## Routing Date Selection
+
+Production watershed reads must request the current calendar year and Julian day.
+The reader must select that exact directory key and verify the calendar year,
+rather than equating the number of read calls with the serialized slot index.
+Schema 2 retains 366 serialized slots per year; synthetic non-leap day 366 is
+padding and must not displace the following year's first routing day. The existing
+`wepp-gregorian-legacy-centurial-v1` calendar remains authoritative: this correction
+does not change which days the watershed requests, including centurial day 366.
+
+`hbp_reader_load_next_day` accepts paired optional `requested_year` and
+`requested_day` arguments. Production supplies both. With both absent, sequential
+serialized-slot iteration remains available for inspection and existing callers.
+Supplying only one argument or requesting an absent key fails explicitly without
+advancing the cursor. Production simulation years are consecutive from the shard
+`begin_year`; lookup derives the simulation-year index from that origin and
+verifies the stored calendar year before returning a payload. A successful dated read positions the sequential cursor
+immediately after the selected record. Exact selection applies to all payload
+fields, including event metadata, tile, groundwater and sediment, for both supported
+schema majors. No file-format, quantization or event-filter change is introduced.
+
+The rationale is to preserve the fixed-slot storage contract while restoring
+routing's date ownership. Dropping writer padding or changing leap rules would
+expand the correction into a format/calendar migration.
+
