+# Mode-2 binary PASS bridge
+
+`src/hbp_mode2_bridge.f90` connects the validated binary PASS reader to existing
+watershed COMMON arrays through `wb12_hbp_mode2_bridge_context`. Open validates
+the complete shard set; metadata seeds hillslope areas and checks particle count.
+Close releases reader state and optionally prints profiling counters.
+
+`hbp_mode2_read_day` receives the current routing calendar year and Julian day
+from `wshred` (`cupdate.year` and `cupdate.sdate`). It requests that exact key from
+`hbp_reader_load_next_day`, fills runoff/lateral/tile/sediment/groundwater arrays,
+and maps the maximum event enum to EVENT, SUBEVENT or NO EVENT. Reader errors are
+returned through `ok` and `message`; `wshred` stops rather than substituting data.
+
+The bridge does not derive a calendar, integrate fluxes, alter precision, or
+change PASS payloads. Schema-2 padding remains serialized but is not consumed
+as a different requested date. Profiling counts successful routing reads, not
+serialized slots. The normative contract is
+[the watershed reader contract](../../contracts/watershed-hillslope-pass-reader-contract.md#routing-date-selection).
